@@ -209,3 +209,33 @@ In `demo` mode (`AI_PROVIDER=demo`), the system runs deterministically without a
    ```powershell
    Invoke-RestMethod -Uri "http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/leads" -Headers @{"X-Admin-Key"="demo-admin-key"}
    ```
+
+---
+
+## 8. Platform integration (added for the one-platform build)
+
+Additive only: no existing route, field or test changed behaviour. Migration `c7d1a2b3e4f5` adds `leads.external_ref`, `leads.details` and a `contact_events` table.
+
+### New canonical endpoints (X-Admin-Key)
+
+| Endpoint | Purpose |
+|---|---|
+| `PATCH /api/v1/leads/{lead_id}` | Update `stage`, `intent`, `owner`, `next_action`, `next_action_date`, `fit_score`, `fit_reasons`, `consent`, `opted_out`. Each change is written to the audit trail. Optional `X-Actor` header names the tool. |
+| `GET/POST /api/v1/leads/{lead_id}/contacts` | Message history on any channel (`channel`, `direction`, `status`, `message_id`, `text`, `timestamp`). A repeated `message_id` is stored once. |
+| `GET /api/v1/funnel` | Counts by stage, source and intent, plus opted-out total. |
+| `GET /api/v1/reminders/due` | Scheduled site visits needing a 24-hour or 2-hour reminder that has not been recorded yet. |
+| `GET /platform` | One dashboard for every tool's leads, with history and audit trail. |
+
+Scheduling, completing or cancelling a site visit now also moves the lead's `stage` (`visit_booked`, `visit_completed`, `visit_cancelled`).
+
+### Adapters (so other tools work without code changes)
+
+All use `Authorization: Bearer <INTEGRATION_API_KEY>` except the public landing form.
+
+| Tool | Point the tool at | Mapping |
+|---|---|---|
+| Avinash's chat (`DB_API_URL`) | `http://<host>/integrations/chat` | `/leads/upsert` creates or updates one lead per conversation (`external_ref = chat:<id>`), matched to existing leads by the 3-step dedupe. `client_id`, `property_type`, timeline, budget (lakh to INR) and role are mapped; intent comes from the shared hot/warm/cold rule; chat-only fields are kept in `details.chat`. Older or same-second records never wipe newer answers. `/messages` stores chat lines with `status: "chat"` so they never count toward the WhatsApp frequency cap. |
+| Tanmayi's engage (`SHARED_DB_URL`) | `http://<host>/integrations/whatsapp` | Same paths her `sharedDbClient.js` already calls: `/api/leads`, `/api/leads/{id}` (GET, PATCH), `/api/leads/{id}/contacts`. |
+| Shalini's landing forms (`FORM_ENDPOINT`) | `http://<host>/integrations/landing/enquiry` | Site-visit and enquiry forms become `source: landing_page` with UTM fields. Referral forms become a `referral` buyer lead (consent kept false until a person confirms) or a `broker` lead for partner sign-ups. Browser origins are limited by `ALLOWED_ORIGINS`. |
+
+New settings: `INTEGRATION_API_KEY` (default `demo-integration-key`) and `ALLOWED_ORIGINS`. Change both, and `ADMIN_API_KEY`, before running anywhere public.
